<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Volsci</h1><p class="st-meta">600 BCE – 304 BCE (approx.) · capital Antium</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Italic people of southern Latium who raided and fought Rome for two centuries, the enemies of the legendary Coriolanus.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Volsci spoke an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osco-umbrian-languages">Osco-Umbrian</a> language and appear in the late 6th century BCE moving from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apennines">Apennines</a> into the Lepini mountains, the Liri valley and the Pontine plain. They took over existing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> towns such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/velletri">Velitrae</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satricum">Satricum</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antium">Antium</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/terracina">Anxur</a> (Tarracina) on the coast.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Volsci formed a loose group of towns rather than a unified state, cooperating in war, often alongside the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/aequi">Aequi</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antium">Antium</a> was a port with a fleet that raided the coast. Their language is known chiefly from a bronze tablet from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/velletri">Velitrae</a>. Roman legend made them the people among whom the exiled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gnaeus-marcius-coriolanus">Gnaeus Marcius Coriolanus</a> took refuge before leading them against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Wars with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latins">Latins</a> continued through the 5th and 4th centuries BCE. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin-war">Latin War</a> Rome took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antium">Antium</a> in 338 BCE and displayed the beaks (rostra) of its warships in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-forum">Forum</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/privernum">Privernum</a> fell in 329 BCE and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sora-lazio">Sora</a> in the following decades, and by about 304 BCE the Volsci had been absorbed.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/volsci.jpg" alt="Volsci" width="320" height="212"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Maduixa assumed (based on copyright claims). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Volsci.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>600 BCE – 304 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Antium</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Volscian polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Volscian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Italy</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Volscians</dd></dl></aside></div>

